1
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:09,989
All right, classes are starting!
Back to your classrooms!

2
00:00:10,073 --> 00:00:11,699
Come on, hurry!

3
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:13,201
Hurry up, come on!

4
00:00:16,454 --> 00:00:18,289
Get back to class!

5
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,926
That hurts!

6
00:00:30,009 --> 00:00:33,596
Hey, everyone, Mr. Shibata hit Sho!

7
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:34,639
What?!

8
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:40,311
What's happening?

9
00:00:57,162 --> 00:01:01,332
Habu, I’m really curious about that.
You're always--

10
00:01:01,416 --> 00:01:03,376
Good morning.

11
00:01:04,377 --> 00:01:08,381
Apologies for the delayed greeting.
My name is Aso, and I’m a lawyer.

12
00:01:08,882 --> 00:01:11,885
Good morning, Ms. Aso.
You look lovely today too.

13
00:01:12,844 --> 00:01:13,845
Thank you very much.

14
00:01:13,928 --> 00:01:17,891
-Do you have a boyfriend?
-Shut up. It's nice meeting you too.

15
00:01:17,974 --> 00:01:19,642
I'll introduce you. Follow me.

16
00:01:19,726 --> 00:01:20,894
-Mr. Kureta!
-Yes!

17
00:01:20,977 --> 00:01:22,645
Over there is our director, Mr. Kureta.

18
00:01:22,729 --> 00:01:23,646
Hello there.

19
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:26,149
Ms. Konno handles
accounting and general tasks.

20
00:01:26,232 --> 00:01:27,400
Nice to meet you.

21
00:01:27,483 --> 00:01:31,154
And I’m Sabayama, a first-class architect,
just like the director.

22
00:01:31,237 --> 00:01:34,282
This is our assistant, Habu.

23
00:01:34,365 --> 00:01:35,533
I’m Kota Habu.

24
00:01:35,617 --> 00:01:38,620
I’m just an assistant,
but I’m better at the job than Sabayama.

25
00:01:38,703 --> 00:01:41,289
Hey, I'm your senior,
call me Mr. Sabayama!

26
00:01:41,372 --> 00:01:44,667
I’m Nakazaki, a part-timer.
I study law at Risshu University.

27
00:01:44,751 --> 00:01:45,960
You study law?

28
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:50,506
I tried to get a job at the law firm,
but I ended up working here.

29
00:01:51,716 --> 00:01:54,677
Oh, Ms. Aso. Would you like
something to drink? Have a seat.

30
00:01:54,761 --> 00:01:56,596
-No, I'm fine.
-Maybe some coffee?

31
00:01:56,679 --> 00:01:58,473
-I'm fine--
-Excuse me…

32
00:01:59,265 --> 00:02:03,436
Is this Mr. Uramawashi's office?

33
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:07,023
Oh, yes. But for now, he's suspended…

34
00:02:07,106 --> 00:02:12,570
For the house of Mr. and Mrs. Shimizu,
let's use a tensegrity structure.

35
00:02:13,196 --> 00:02:16,866
The ceiling will look otherworldly.

36
00:02:18,785 --> 00:02:21,663
Excuse me, are you Mr. Uramawashi?

37
00:02:22,372 --> 00:02:23,790
What can I do for you?

38
00:02:24,874 --> 00:02:27,961
Please help my father.

39
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:39,389
My father teaches at Karasawa Junior High,

40
00:02:39,889 --> 00:02:42,267
and he hit a student.

41
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,394
<i>Hey, everyone, Mr. Shibata hit Sho!</i>

42
00:02:44,477 --> 00:02:47,355
The student's parents
filed a police report,

43
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:49,357
and my father was arrested.

44
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,360
Do you know why he resorted to violence?

45
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:57,490
He said he was just warning them
about their messy attire,

46
00:02:58,157 --> 00:03:01,327
but he's not the type of man
to hit someone just for that.

47
00:03:01,411 --> 00:03:03,538
Is there anything else you can think of?

48
00:03:03,621 --> 00:03:06,874
No, he wouldn't tell me anything.

49
00:03:08,459 --> 00:03:13,047
That's when I found Mr. Uramawashi's
business card on my father's desk.

50
00:03:19,762 --> 00:03:21,931
I must save my father!

51
00:03:22,015 --> 00:03:24,892
I'll pay you,
even if it takes my whole life.

52
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:26,060
Please!

53
00:03:30,273 --> 00:03:33,359
Your love for your father is touching.

54
00:03:33,443 --> 00:03:36,654
However, I'm currently suspended.

55
00:03:36,738 --> 00:03:39,949
If I have any contact with clients,
it would be a violation,

56
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:43,077
and Ms. Aso here will report me.

57
00:03:43,161 --> 00:03:44,078
No, I--

58
00:03:44,162 --> 00:03:46,831
I’m sorry I can’t be of help.

59
00:03:49,417 --> 00:03:50,585
Understood.

60
00:03:58,926 --> 00:04:00,094
Please wait!

61
00:04:02,388 --> 00:04:05,350
If you don't mind, I can help you.

62
00:04:08,519 --> 00:04:09,937
Thank you very much.

63
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:20,323
You don't see passionate teachers
like him much nowadays.

64
00:04:20,406 --> 00:04:22,241
Used to be lots of them back in the day.

65
00:04:22,325 --> 00:04:25,244
Mr. Uramawashi,
I am the defense counsel for this case.

66
00:04:25,328 --> 00:04:29,582
I’m just stating my personal opinion.
My view on this is…

67
00:04:29,665 --> 00:04:31,167
That’s quite enough.

68
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:32,627
Do you dislike me?

69
00:04:33,336 --> 00:04:35,338
It’s not about liking or disliking.

70
00:04:36,005 --> 00:04:39,384
You are currently suspended, right?

71
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:44,138
Besides, Mr. Uramawashi, you and I have
completely different mindsets as lawyers.

72
00:04:44,222 --> 00:04:45,181
Mindsets?

73
00:04:45,264 --> 00:04:48,142
In my life so far,
I have never told a single lie.

74
00:04:48,226 --> 00:04:49,811
Such a person actually exists?

75
00:04:49,894 --> 00:04:52,063
You're supposed to laugh.

76
00:04:52,146 --> 00:04:53,856
I’m not joking.

77
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,776
It's meaningless
to win something through a lie.

78
00:04:57,318 --> 00:04:59,654
When I’m about to lie, I wait six seconds.

79
00:04:59,737 --> 00:05:02,990
Then the lie starts to feel ridiculous.

80
00:05:03,074 --> 00:05:08,329
-One, two, three, four…
-What?

81
00:05:08,413 --> 00:05:11,249
-What? Wait…
-Five, six.

82
00:05:12,208 --> 00:05:15,628
What a coincidence. I hate lies too.

83
00:05:18,297 --> 00:05:21,134
The effect varies from person to person.

84
00:05:21,884 --> 00:05:24,637
Sometimes a lie is necessary
to unravel another lie.

85
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:29,642
No, you destroy lies with the truth!

86
00:05:29,725 --> 00:05:32,895
You are like
the Christchurch Cardboard Cathedral.

87
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:35,356
-Nice one.
-Another architecture reference?

88
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,358
He means you're stronger than you look.

89
00:05:38,609 --> 00:05:39,819
That's enough.

90
00:05:39,902 --> 00:05:42,822
You and I
will never understand each other.

91
00:05:43,406 --> 00:05:44,323
Whoa!

92
00:05:44,949 --> 00:05:47,827
-What's going on?
-Move aside!

93
00:05:49,912 --> 00:05:50,746
Go on!

94
00:05:51,581 --> 00:05:53,708
What is this all of a sudden?

95
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:56,544
-Aso, record this.
-Huh?

96
00:05:56,627 --> 00:05:57,712
Hurry up.

97
00:05:57,795 --> 00:06:01,674
Huh? Look, this is too sudden…

98
00:06:01,757 --> 00:06:03,467
Hang on… Okay.

99
00:06:04,051 --> 00:06:08,014
No, maybe this angle is better. Wait…

100
00:06:11,017 --> 00:06:12,685
What just came over you?

101
00:06:12,768 --> 00:06:14,604
-Show me.
-Okay.

102
00:06:14,687 --> 00:06:16,480
-I want to see!
-Here.

103
00:06:17,773 --> 00:06:20,109
<i>No, maybe this angle is better.</i>

104
00:06:20,193 --> 00:06:21,485
What do you think?

105
00:06:22,612 --> 00:06:24,113
You two are pretty good.

106
00:06:24,197 --> 00:06:28,326
-Right?
-We were trying to copy Monaki.

107
00:06:28,409 --> 00:06:31,746
-I see.
-That’s not what you should be looking at.

108
00:06:31,829 --> 00:06:33,206
Huh?

109
00:06:33,289 --> 00:06:34,624
Hey, that's…

110
00:06:34,707 --> 00:06:36,375
<i>No, maybe…</i>

111
00:06:36,459 --> 00:06:39,629
At the beginning of the video,
the camera is shaky.

112
00:06:39,712 --> 00:06:43,257
Well, that's because you suddenly
told me to start filming.

113
00:06:43,341 --> 00:06:47,470
Yes, a spontaneous recording
always starts like this.

114
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:55,102
Wait, excuse me!

115
00:06:55,186 --> 00:06:58,231
FLAMING MONSTER

116
00:06:58,314 --> 00:07:01,817
The video of Mr. Shibata was stable.

117
00:07:01,901 --> 00:07:04,528
Someone set up a camera in advance!

118
00:07:06,155 --> 00:07:07,740
Hey, I have to go!

119
00:07:10,201 --> 00:07:13,621
Hey, don't do anything on your own, okay?

120
00:07:13,704 --> 00:07:15,373
I'll focus on my work.

121
00:07:15,456 --> 00:07:20,920
Right now, you are an architect,
not a lawyer. Got that? An architect!

122
00:07:23,548 --> 00:07:25,174
All right, everyone,

123
00:07:26,259 --> 00:07:28,261
time to expose the lie.

124
00:08:10,678 --> 00:08:12,763
May I ask who you are?

125
00:08:12,847 --> 00:08:16,559
I apologize for the sudden visit.
My name is Aso, and I’m a lawyer.

126
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:19,395
I have questions
about Mr. Shibata's case--

127
00:08:19,478 --> 00:08:21,147
We have nothing to tell you!

128
00:08:22,273 --> 00:08:26,360
There’s a possibility that the video
of Mr. Shibata was staged!

129
00:08:29,071 --> 00:08:32,450
Mrs. Shimoyama, can you talk to me?

130
00:08:39,248 --> 00:08:45,838
SCHOOL ROUTE
ITABASHI WARD

131
00:08:47,214 --> 00:08:48,633
Goodbye.

132
00:08:51,177 --> 00:08:52,845
-Hello.
-Be careful!

133
00:08:52,928 --> 00:08:55,681
-I'm here to see the principal.
-Go ahead.

134
00:09:01,103 --> 00:09:03,814
CONGRATULATIONS SOCCER TEAM!
TOURNAMENT PARTICIPANTS

135
00:09:08,778 --> 00:09:11,238
Mr. Uramawashi, why are you here?

136
00:09:11,322 --> 00:09:14,867
If you get caught,
I'll be held responsible!

137
00:09:14,950 --> 00:09:17,286
The Tacoma Narrows Bridge
in Washington State

138
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:21,248
was built without sufficient testing,
and so, after only four months,

139
00:09:22,541 --> 00:09:23,709
it collapsed.

140
00:09:25,211 --> 00:09:28,005
I have no idea what you're talking about,
but please wait.

141
00:09:28,089 --> 00:09:30,257
Please wait!

142
00:09:30,341 --> 00:09:32,551
Are you a rabbit?

143
00:09:32,635 --> 00:09:35,888
Listen, you must not use lies.

144
00:09:35,971 --> 00:09:38,265
I will fight fair and square and win.

145
00:09:38,349 --> 00:09:41,018
I'll store the lies away in the basement.

146
00:09:42,687 --> 00:09:44,021
Thank you for today.

147
00:09:44,105 --> 00:09:45,564
Thank you for coming.

148
00:09:46,357 --> 00:09:49,902
That person over there
is Assembly Member Miku Nijima, right?

149
00:09:49,985 --> 00:09:51,862
If I recall, she’s a former idol…

150
00:09:51,946 --> 00:09:56,367
From Pastel Sugar!
I loved them back when I was a kid!

151
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:58,786
I’m going to use the restroom.
Go on ahead.

152
00:09:58,869 --> 00:09:59,912
What?

153
00:10:02,623 --> 00:10:04,500
He's in his own world.

154
00:10:05,167 --> 00:10:08,671
That is strictly
Mr. Shibata’s personal issue.

155
00:10:09,422 --> 00:10:13,426
Please don't make it a problem
with our school's management system.

156
00:10:14,301 --> 00:10:19,807
Mr. Shibata had recently been
actively opposing the school merger.

157
00:10:21,225 --> 00:10:23,602
It seems he had been
building up a lot of stress.

158
00:10:23,686 --> 00:10:25,479
He was opposing a merger?

159
00:10:25,563 --> 00:10:28,065
Was he having trouble
with anyone because of that?

160
00:10:28,149 --> 00:10:31,527
No, nothing comes to mind, but…

161
00:10:32,737 --> 00:10:35,322
Representative Nijima
was also here for the merger?

162
00:10:35,406 --> 00:10:39,076
Yes, we asked her here for her opinions.

163
00:10:40,619 --> 00:10:44,790
Excuse me. I would like to ask you
about this video of Sho Shimoyama.

164
00:10:44,874 --> 00:10:46,500
I don't know anything about it.

165
00:10:46,584 --> 00:10:48,502
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

166
00:10:49,253 --> 00:10:53,007
-What was she asking you about?
-About the video.

167
00:10:57,136 --> 00:10:59,805
School merger, huh?

168
00:11:02,516 --> 00:11:04,018
Wait, where did he go?

169
00:11:05,227 --> 00:11:07,229
MR. URAMAWASHI
MEET ME AT CLASS 3-1

170
00:11:10,775 --> 00:11:14,528
Geez! What are you doing…

171
00:11:14,612 --> 00:11:19,575
Let me introduce you to the person
who filmed our viral video.

172
00:11:19,658 --> 00:11:21,702
Taiga Takanashi.

173
00:11:22,786 --> 00:11:25,122
How did you know it was him?

174
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:27,875
I guessed the filming location
from the video’s angle,

175
00:11:28,751 --> 00:11:30,377
and it led to his seat.

176
00:11:32,213 --> 00:11:35,090
Takanashi is the ace of the soccer team,

177
00:11:35,174 --> 00:11:39,428
so everyone was too scared
of him to speak up.

178
00:11:40,429 --> 00:11:41,263
Am I right?

179
00:11:45,976 --> 00:11:48,437
Would you mind telling us about it?

180
00:11:49,438 --> 00:11:52,525
It's nothing much.
I just filmed Sho by accident.

181
00:11:52,608 --> 00:11:54,568
But you set up your camera in advance.

182
00:11:54,652 --> 00:11:56,362
I did no such thing.

183
00:11:57,154 --> 00:11:58,656
If you don't mind,

184
00:11:59,907 --> 00:12:04,411
I would like to see the video.

185
00:12:24,265 --> 00:12:25,766
Are you okay?

186
00:12:26,517 --> 00:12:28,018
Hold on!

187
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,360
Stop!

188
00:12:37,361 --> 00:12:38,988
I'm sorry, are you okay?

189
00:12:39,905 --> 00:12:41,949
Wait for me!

190
00:12:50,874 --> 00:12:52,126
How?

191
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:58,090
Know the layout of the school building,
and you can predict the escape routes.

192
00:12:58,173 --> 00:12:59,550
Mr. Uramawashi?!

193
00:12:59,633 --> 00:13:01,594
How did you beat me here?

194
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:05,264
Don't be so on guard.

195
00:13:05,973 --> 00:13:07,516
You forgot something.

196
00:13:08,309 --> 00:13:09,977
I just want to return it to you.

197
00:13:10,561 --> 00:13:12,855
-My phone!
-When you bumped into me…

198
00:13:12,938 --> 00:13:15,190
You dropped it…

199
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:27,911
In the end, we couldn't
get anything out of Mr. Takanashi.

200
00:13:27,995 --> 00:13:33,292
Well then, shall we take a look
at the original video he recorded?

201
00:13:33,375 --> 00:13:35,294
You have the video?

202
00:13:36,128 --> 00:13:39,006
I went through his phone's data
before returning it.

203
00:13:39,089 --> 00:13:41,634
Is that even legal?

204
00:13:48,557 --> 00:13:51,769
So it's because he was smoking.

205
00:13:51,852 --> 00:13:55,356
If a student is found smoking,
it may affect his prospects.

206
00:13:55,439 --> 00:13:59,610
So Mr. Shibata lied and said
it was just about messy clothes.

207
00:13:59,693 --> 00:14:01,487
Do you think lying here is wrong?

208
00:14:03,989 --> 00:14:06,659
Underage smoking is against the law.

209
00:14:06,742 --> 00:14:10,371
Even middle schoolers must be responsible.

210
00:14:11,372 --> 00:14:16,669
So, where do you think
underage smokers usually smoke?

211
00:14:16,752 --> 00:14:18,337
I guess…

212
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:19,672
Behind the gymnasium.

213
00:14:20,714 --> 00:14:25,761
You're right. But in the video,
he is smoking out in the open!

214
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:30,808
Come to think of it,
I got a call from my son Taiga earlier.

215
00:14:30,891 --> 00:14:33,936
He said a young lawyer
came to question him.

216
00:14:34,019 --> 00:14:37,064
-That must be Ms. Aso.
-Bingo!

217
00:14:37,147 --> 00:14:39,108
What about the video?
It hasn't been found out yet?

218
00:14:39,191 --> 00:14:42,236
-He said he didn't tell her anything.
-Then it's fine.

219
00:14:42,319 --> 00:14:46,740
If the school merger goes through,
it will be your achievement, Ms. Nijima.

220
00:14:46,824 --> 00:14:51,036
Yes. Otherwise,
we'll have a problem, Mr. Hyuga.

221
00:14:52,121 --> 00:14:57,042
Please make sure you choose
my company to be your contractor,

222
00:14:57,126 --> 00:14:58,252
Mr. Takanashi.

223
00:14:58,335 --> 00:15:03,632
Of course.
Do well, and we'll reward you richly.

224
00:15:07,261 --> 00:15:09,138
It's just as you said, Ms. Aso.

225
00:15:10,139 --> 00:15:13,642
When I searched the house,
I found the signatures.

226
00:15:22,526 --> 00:15:24,194
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

227
00:15:24,278 --> 00:15:26,822
He got so many people to sign.

228
00:15:28,032 --> 00:15:29,158
But…

229
00:15:29,908 --> 00:15:31,618
With my father arrested,

230
00:15:32,244 --> 00:15:35,956
it seems the opposition
has been greatly weakened.

231
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,291
Really?

232
00:15:39,001 --> 00:15:41,837
They say they can't side
with a violent teacher.

233
00:15:43,464 --> 00:15:46,008
But my father isn't that kind of person…

234
00:15:49,053 --> 00:15:51,305
I’ll look into it as well.

235
00:15:55,684 --> 00:15:59,730
Regarding Nijima, who Mr. Uramawashi
spotted at Karasawa Junior High,

236
00:15:59,813 --> 00:16:01,732
I checked her social media.

237
00:16:02,733 --> 00:16:04,151
She's a huge fan of Monaki!

238
00:16:04,234 --> 00:16:05,861
That's irrelevant!

239
00:16:05,944 --> 00:16:10,783
She was accused online of having affairs,
and having done nothing of note.

240
00:16:10,866 --> 00:16:14,828
So she wants to push for the school merger
and win some votes.

241
00:16:14,912 --> 00:16:16,705
-Hey, show the next one.
-Okay.

242
00:16:17,539 --> 00:16:20,417
The father of Taiga Takanashi,
who shot the video,

243
00:16:20,501 --> 00:16:22,836
is the CEO
of a major construction company.

244
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:28,133
Public works projects offer good money,
so he wouldn't want the merger to fail.

245
00:16:28,217 --> 00:16:31,970
However, it seems the real goal
isn't just the school merger.

246
00:16:32,054 --> 00:16:32,888
Huh?

247
00:16:33,514 --> 00:16:35,599
The redevelopment plan for Itabashi Ward.

248
00:16:35,682 --> 00:16:38,852
The land adjacent to Karasawa Junior High
is also in that area.

249
00:16:38,936 --> 00:16:41,063
If they become the main developers,

250
00:16:41,146 --> 00:16:44,191
they can make a lot more money
than just tearing down a school.

251
00:16:44,274 --> 00:16:47,361
So, they framed Mr. Shibata for this?

252
00:16:47,444 --> 00:16:51,740
He was leading the opposition,
but still, he's just a teacher.

253
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:55,244
-Sorry, I’m late.
-Habu, you!

254
00:16:55,327 --> 00:16:59,331
-I told you to be here at four!
-Unlike you, I was actually working.

255
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,208
-Here.
-Okay.

256
00:17:01,291 --> 00:17:02,918
Show us what you got!

257
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:07,840
Ms. Manami handed the opposition
signatures Mr. Shibata collected

258
00:17:08,423 --> 00:17:09,842
over to Ms. Aso.

259
00:17:09,925 --> 00:17:12,803
-Did you photograph the signature file?
-Of course I did.

260
00:17:15,681 --> 00:17:17,057
-Not bad.
-Next slide.

261
00:17:18,392 --> 00:17:20,519
Oh, sorry.

262
00:17:22,646 --> 00:17:26,900
I was adjusting the focus.

263
00:17:30,445 --> 00:17:32,739
You only took photos of Ms. Aso!

264
00:17:38,036 --> 00:17:40,956
-This is the file.
-Don't try to play it off!

265
00:17:41,039 --> 00:17:43,083
A direct demand petition.

266
00:17:43,167 --> 00:17:46,086
This would force the assembly
to discuss the issue, right?

267
00:17:46,170 --> 00:17:52,050
And Nijima didn't want it submitted,
so she tried to get rid of Mr. Shibata?

268
00:17:52,134 --> 00:17:54,845
To destroy the opposition's main pillar.

269
00:17:54,928 --> 00:17:58,891
But an ex-idol representative,
and a company CEO?

270
00:17:58,974 --> 00:18:00,517
Isn't this too elaborate?

271
00:18:00,601 --> 00:18:03,145
Perhaps there's a hidden mastermind?

272
00:18:03,687 --> 00:18:05,856
Maybe this lawyer.

273
00:18:05,939 --> 00:18:07,065
ATSUMU HYUGA

274
00:18:07,149 --> 00:18:08,025
His lies.

275
00:18:09,067 --> 00:18:10,402
I'll expose them.

276
00:18:12,154 --> 00:18:15,574
Mr. Uramawashi has not been
up to any problematic behavior so far.

277
00:18:15,657 --> 00:18:17,951
What do you mean
by "problematic behavior"?

278
00:18:18,035 --> 00:18:19,369
For example…

279
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:29,463
He hasn't been doing any investigations
or contacting any clients on his own.

280
00:18:29,546 --> 00:18:31,757
I see. Not "on his own."

281
00:18:32,424 --> 00:18:33,926
Also, actually,

282
00:18:34,009 --> 00:18:39,139
I took on a new case from a client
I met at Mr. Uramawashi's office.

283
00:18:43,644 --> 00:18:45,270
There's no problem with that.

284
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:48,357
Thank you.

285
00:18:50,484 --> 00:18:53,987
It's okay. I'm okay…

286
00:18:54,071 --> 00:18:57,032
I wasn't lying.

287
00:18:57,115 --> 00:18:59,576
He didn't do
any of those things "on his own"!

288
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:02,871
That's right, I didn't lie.

289
00:19:02,955 --> 00:19:04,957
So you two are working together?

290
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:09,086
As part of my supervision, I need
to keep him within sight. Nothing more.

291
00:19:09,169 --> 00:19:11,630
Part of your supervision, I see.

292
00:19:11,713 --> 00:19:14,466
Did you take on another troublesome case?

293
00:19:14,549 --> 00:19:17,469
A middle school teacher ended up
using violence on a student.

294
00:19:17,552 --> 00:19:19,012
Corporal punishment.

295
00:19:19,805 --> 00:19:22,349
Prohibited under Education Code,
Article 11.

296
00:19:22,432 --> 00:19:24,226
This is clearly an assault case.

297
00:19:24,309 --> 00:19:26,603
I would like to reach
a settlement somehow,

298
00:19:26,687 --> 00:19:29,231
but the merger is complicating things.

299
00:19:29,314 --> 00:19:31,900
With a school merger,

300
00:19:31,984 --> 00:19:34,486
you would think teachers and parents
would end up on the same side.

301
00:19:34,569 --> 00:19:35,946
The same side?

302
00:19:36,029 --> 00:19:40,450
I mean, the school being torn down
would normally be something no one wants.

303
00:20:34,254 --> 00:20:35,380
STUDENT ROSTER

304
00:20:57,986 --> 00:21:02,240
Time to overwrite this blueprint of lies.

305
00:21:09,748 --> 00:21:11,208
Good morning.

306
00:21:11,291 --> 00:21:14,336
Morning Ms. Aso.
Mr. Uramawashi is sleeping.

307
00:21:14,419 --> 00:21:17,422
-Sleeping?
-He pulled an all-nighter.

308
00:21:18,131 --> 00:21:19,299
Must be nice.

309
00:21:19,383 --> 00:21:21,885
I pulled an all-nighter too.
I'm so sleepy.

310
00:21:22,552 --> 00:21:24,805
Then why don't you try using this?

311
00:21:25,806 --> 00:21:26,848
An eye mask?

312
00:21:26,932 --> 00:21:29,518
Yeah, my recommendation.
It's new, so don't worry.

313
00:21:29,601 --> 00:21:31,436
Thank you very much.

314
00:21:34,731 --> 00:21:36,400
-I'm turning it on.
-Okay.

315
00:21:36,983 --> 00:21:38,193
There.

316
00:21:39,528 --> 00:21:43,657
Oh, this feels pretty nice.

317
00:21:44,574 --> 00:21:48,120
Right? A lawyer's body
is their main asset, after all.

318
00:21:48,203 --> 00:21:49,913
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

319
00:21:49,996 --> 00:21:54,626
I don't deny democracy itself.

320
00:21:55,419 --> 00:21:57,379
<i>However, in Japan,</i>

321
00:21:57,462 --> 00:22:01,633
<i>obtaining everyone's consensus</i>
<i>takes a lot of time.</i>

322
00:22:01,716 --> 00:22:06,138
<i>And the world will have moved on</i>
<i>to the next stage.</i>

323
00:22:06,221 --> 00:22:08,223
<i>What I want to say is…</i>

324
00:22:09,015 --> 00:22:13,270
<i>What this country needs right now</i>
<i>is speedy decision-making.</i>

325
00:22:13,353 --> 00:22:16,606
Furuse is as popular as ever, huh.

326
00:22:16,690 --> 00:22:22,320
His stance is a bit forceful,
but it's what Japan needs right now.

327
00:22:22,404 --> 00:22:24,865
He makes you nervous in person.

328
00:22:24,948 --> 00:22:26,491
His presence is intense.

329
00:22:27,325 --> 00:22:30,996
And all I did was greet him
at a party meeting!

330
00:22:31,746 --> 00:22:35,041
If we score an achievement
and get close to him,

331
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:37,502
soon we'll be in national politics.

332
00:22:40,297 --> 00:22:43,633
Excuse me.
You have a call from a Mr. Imai.

333
00:22:43,717 --> 00:22:47,137
Imai? I don't know anyone
by that name, though.

334
00:22:47,220 --> 00:22:50,056
They said it's about
the opposition to the school merger.

335
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:53,727
WHAT DOES JAPANESE POLITICS NEED?

336
00:22:57,522 --> 00:23:01,276
Hello! Nijima speaking.

337
00:23:01,359 --> 00:23:04,237
<i>Mr. Furuse, will you carry that role?</i>

338
00:23:04,321 --> 00:23:07,032
<i>If the citizens desire it,</i>

339
00:23:07,115 --> 00:23:09,618
<i>I am prepared</i>
<i>to carry that responsibility.</i>

340
00:23:10,118 --> 00:23:15,707
<i>Of course, there is pushback</i>
<i>to any reform. Criticism too.</i>

341
00:23:15,790 --> 00:23:18,668
<i>However, because we feared criticism</i>

342
00:23:18,752 --> 00:23:23,465
<i>and kept postponing decisions,</i>
<i>Japan ended up where it is today.</i>

343
00:23:28,595 --> 00:23:32,349
What are you here to talk about?

344
00:23:32,432 --> 00:23:33,850
Well…

345
00:23:33,934 --> 00:23:36,770
Because of the recent violent incident,

346
00:23:36,853 --> 00:23:40,148
some residents are more drawn
to supporting the merger.

347
00:23:40,815 --> 00:23:42,567
The ones who used to oppose it?

348
00:23:43,568 --> 00:23:47,614
However, there are still
many residents on the fence,

349
00:23:47,697 --> 00:23:51,534
so if we provide the venue,
can you host an informational meeting?

350
00:23:51,618 --> 00:23:53,995
An explanatory meeting?

351
00:23:54,079 --> 00:23:56,373
Yes, they just need one final push.

352
00:23:56,456 --> 00:23:58,750
Is that story really true?

353
00:23:59,459 --> 00:24:02,087
Do you mean I'm lying?

354
00:24:02,754 --> 00:24:08,426
Maybe you plan to stall us by making us do
a meeting where no one intends to listen.

355
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:10,220
A trap by the opposition?

356
00:24:10,303 --> 00:24:12,055
That's not true.

357
00:24:18,853 --> 00:24:21,439
Look, I have proof.

358
00:24:21,523 --> 00:24:22,399
SIGNATURES

359
00:24:22,482 --> 00:24:26,486
These are the signatures for the petition
that Mr. Shibata was gathering.

360
00:24:27,279 --> 00:24:28,738
Excuse me.

361
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:37,539
This doesn't look like…

362
00:24:38,206 --> 00:24:39,874
a copy.

363
00:24:39,958 --> 00:24:41,710
It's definitely the real thing.

364
00:24:44,129 --> 00:24:48,758
If we succeed in persuading
the opposition, even the relocation fees…

365
00:24:52,554 --> 00:24:56,016
Understood.
Let's hold the explanatory meeting.

366
00:24:56,099 --> 00:24:57,600
Thank you very much.

367
00:24:57,684 --> 00:24:59,060
If you'll excuse me.

368
00:24:59,144 --> 00:25:00,687
Wait, please.

369
00:25:00,770 --> 00:25:02,939
Please leave the signatures with me.

370
00:25:03,023 --> 00:25:04,065
What?

371
00:25:04,149 --> 00:25:06,401
If you're leaving the opposition,
it should be no issue.

372
00:25:13,199 --> 00:25:14,242
Okay.

373
00:25:15,535 --> 00:25:17,996
I'll be expecting
the relocation fee, then.

374
00:25:18,705 --> 00:25:20,457
Thank you very much.

375
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:26,046
You took photos
of all the signatures, right?

376
00:25:26,129 --> 00:25:27,630
<i>Yes, just in case.</i>

377
00:25:27,714 --> 00:25:29,466
Recreate them right now.

378
00:25:29,549 --> 00:25:30,842
<i>Huh? Why?</i>

379
00:25:30,925 --> 00:25:34,387
Please, I'm begging you.
Ms. Aso will kill me.

380
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:40,310
The opposition was surprisingly stubborn.

381
00:25:40,810 --> 00:25:44,981
There is no way they can gather
enough signatures with just one week left.

382
00:25:47,067 --> 00:25:51,905
BREAK THE HYPOCRITICAL TRIO'S PLAN

383
00:25:53,865 --> 00:25:56,910
This is the schedule
for the three of them.

384
00:25:59,454 --> 00:26:02,332
-There's no day when all three are free.
-What do we do?

385
00:26:02,415 --> 00:26:04,459
Handling them separately is impossible.

386
00:26:04,542 --> 00:26:05,752
What now?

387
00:26:08,421 --> 00:26:09,381
What about here?

388
00:26:09,464 --> 00:26:13,468
I can't make it on this day.
I've also been invited to this wedding.

389
00:26:14,135 --> 00:26:16,638
Hyuga and Nijima…

390
00:26:18,473 --> 00:26:20,225
Should we invite them there?

391
00:26:20,725 --> 00:26:23,895
THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN THE THREE

392
00:26:23,978 --> 00:26:25,522
Congratulations.

393
00:26:26,022 --> 00:26:28,024
<i>Next up for our bride and groom</i>

394
00:26:28,108 --> 00:26:32,237
<i>is the wedding cake cutting</i>
<i>and the first bite ceremony!</i>

395
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:36,366
How's this? It's all about the vibes.
How about we put it here?

396
00:26:36,449 --> 00:26:38,451
What do you think?

397
00:26:39,828 --> 00:26:42,705
Isn't doing an interview at a wedding
a bit implausible?

398
00:26:42,789 --> 00:26:44,332
Stop complaining and look.

399
00:26:44,416 --> 00:26:47,752
There are many people around,
we'll blend in, and no one will notice.

400
00:26:47,836 --> 00:26:49,671
Minori, let me know if he does anything!

401
00:26:49,754 --> 00:26:51,047
I'll give him a kicking!

402
00:26:51,131 --> 00:26:54,884
<i>Everyone, please give them</i>
<i>a big round of applause!</i>

403
00:26:54,968 --> 00:26:57,470
Takanashi can monitor
from right next to them too.

404
00:26:57,554 --> 00:26:58,805
So, what's the situation?

405
00:26:58,888 --> 00:27:01,182
Nijima is almost done with her makeup.

406
00:27:01,766 --> 00:27:04,060
-Right on time.
-Sorry to keep you waiting.

407
00:27:05,311 --> 00:27:09,023
Allow me to guide you
to the interview room. This way.

408
00:27:10,066 --> 00:27:12,944
They are having an outfit change.
Takanashi's heading over.

409
00:27:15,113 --> 00:27:17,615
I'll show you to the waiting room
on the second floor.

410
00:27:20,618 --> 00:27:21,828
<i>Right now?</i>

411
00:27:23,288 --> 00:27:25,665
They're going to cross paths!

412
00:27:27,834 --> 00:27:29,502
Sorry, Ai.

413
00:27:29,586 --> 00:27:32,630
Nijima and Hyuga
already know what I look like.

414
00:27:33,423 --> 00:27:37,260
Huh? Are you Mikurin from Pastel Sugar?
Please shake my hand!

415
00:27:37,343 --> 00:27:39,429
-Hey…
-Sorry, I'm working.

416
00:27:39,512 --> 00:27:43,266
But I'm a huge fan!
Can I at least get a picture?

417
00:27:44,476 --> 00:27:47,437
-Are you a Monaki fan?
-Yes, I am!

418
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:50,106
Wait, Mikurin, you like Monaki too?

419
00:27:50,190 --> 00:27:51,232
Yes.

420
00:27:52,275 --> 00:27:55,069
Oh, man! Just one picture, please!

421
00:27:55,153 --> 00:27:58,281
-One should be fine.
-Thank you! Over here, please.

422
00:27:58,364 --> 00:28:02,494
I'm so happy right now!
So, who is your favorite?

423
00:28:02,577 --> 00:28:03,620
I like all of them.

424
00:28:03,703 --> 00:28:07,207
-Once ready, the staff will guide you.
-Okay.

425
00:28:07,707 --> 00:28:08,833
Same!

426
00:28:08,917 --> 00:28:12,462
Come on, isn't this schedule
way too tight?

427
00:28:15,048 --> 00:28:18,259
We've been expecting you.
Thank you for your time today.

428
00:28:18,343 --> 00:28:20,220
-Right this way.
-Here.

429
00:28:20,303 --> 00:28:22,347
-The cable!
-Sorry.

430
00:28:25,016 --> 00:28:27,769
-Is here fine?
-Yes, please take a seat.

431
00:28:27,852 --> 00:28:30,939
-We sent you a script…
-I looked at it.

432
00:28:31,564 --> 00:28:33,399
Thank you so much.

433
00:28:34,275 --> 00:28:36,903
Everyone, please be sure to check it out!

434
00:28:37,987 --> 00:28:40,573
Got it! Thank you!

435
00:28:40,657 --> 00:28:44,452
You came out nicely.
You'll be number one, Ms. Nijima.

436
00:28:44,536 --> 00:28:47,330
Well, considering my opposition…

437
00:28:47,413 --> 00:28:49,290
Thank you very much.

438
00:28:49,374 --> 00:28:50,875
-My bag.
-Here.

439
00:28:50,959 --> 00:28:53,461
-Thank you very much.
-This way.

440
00:28:56,256 --> 00:28:58,716
Ms. Nijima is returning
to the waiting room.

441
00:29:00,385 --> 00:29:01,761
Please put this away.

442
00:29:04,931 --> 00:29:08,017
-Good work today!
-Thank you.

443
00:29:08,101 --> 00:29:12,605
-Thank you.
-Hey, what are you doing? Hurry it up.

444
00:29:12,689 --> 00:29:15,608
-I'm sorry. Right this way.
-Yeah.

445
00:29:17,026 --> 00:29:19,904
Wait, I'm not ready yet, hurry!

446
00:29:20,572 --> 00:29:22,448
<i>Hyuga is here!</i>

447
00:29:22,532 --> 00:29:23,658
Hold him off for a sec!

448
00:29:23,741 --> 00:29:27,579
-Mr. Hyuga, we've been waiting for you!
-Oh, hello.

449
00:29:27,662 --> 00:29:30,164
Do you always host interviews
in places like this?

450
00:29:30,248 --> 00:29:33,376
Due to scheduling conflicts,
this was the only venue available…

451
00:29:34,711 --> 00:29:39,132
-Are you thirsty?
-I'm fine. Let's start right away.

452
00:29:39,215 --> 00:29:41,759
-I can't stall him!
-Did you say third floor?

453
00:29:41,843 --> 00:29:43,219
This way, sir.

454
00:29:45,179 --> 00:29:47,098
They're definitely going to cross paths!

455
00:29:47,181 --> 00:29:49,559
-Huh?
-Oh, nothing.

456
00:29:51,811 --> 00:29:54,606
I really wanted to be in this magazine.

457
00:29:54,689 --> 00:29:57,650
I have all the past issues!

458
00:29:58,276 --> 00:30:01,321
Are you Kenji Moriya from Dragon Wash?

459
00:30:01,404 --> 00:30:02,614
No, I'm not.

460
00:30:02,697 --> 00:30:04,407
-What?
-Do I look like him?

461
00:30:04,490 --> 00:30:06,701
You're so cool! You look just like him!

462
00:30:06,784 --> 00:30:10,830
Not hitting on you or anything,
but may I take a picture?

463
00:30:10,914 --> 00:30:12,498
Oh, sure.

464
00:30:12,582 --> 00:30:15,293
Really? Thank you so much! I'm so happy!

465
00:30:15,376 --> 00:30:18,504
<i>Ms. Nijima is heading back too!</i>
<i>Somebody stop her!</i>

466
00:30:22,675 --> 00:30:25,261
Thank you very much.
Please go down these stairs.

467
00:30:25,345 --> 00:30:27,972
-I'm taking the elevator back.
-No, but…

468
00:30:28,056 --> 00:30:30,350
The stairs would be faster!

469
00:30:30,433 --> 00:30:32,769
This elevator is broken.

470
00:30:32,852 --> 00:30:34,354
I think it still works.

471
00:30:39,943 --> 00:30:41,152
After you.

472
00:30:42,695 --> 00:30:44,113
Thank you.

473
00:30:45,156 --> 00:30:47,659
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

474
00:30:50,912 --> 00:30:54,916
I'm really sorry.
I went to the wrong floor.

475
00:30:54,999 --> 00:30:57,001
May I? Thank you so much!

476
00:30:57,085 --> 00:30:59,295
I'm so happy. Here we go.

477
00:30:59,379 --> 00:31:00,546
Say cheese!

478
00:31:00,630 --> 00:31:04,217
So cool!
Wait, can I take a pic of just you?

479
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:06,719
Thank you so much.

480
00:31:06,803 --> 00:31:08,221
Oh, wow!

481
00:31:11,015 --> 00:31:13,518
Nice job, everyone!

482
00:31:14,143 --> 00:31:16,270
Thank you very much.

483
00:31:16,354 --> 00:31:19,107
I think our readers
at <i>Modern Wall </i>will be thrilled

484
00:31:19,190 --> 00:31:21,359
to read about your tips
for a good sleep, sir.

485
00:31:21,442 --> 00:31:24,153
Glad to help.
Feel free to invite me again.

486
00:31:24,237 --> 00:31:26,364
-Thank you very much.
-Bye.

487
00:31:32,912 --> 00:31:35,081
Excuse me. I'm Hyuga.

488
00:31:35,164 --> 00:31:37,875
-Please, come on in. Yes!
-Over there?

489
00:31:38,918 --> 00:31:41,713
I'm Harada from <i>Meow's Week</i>.

490
00:31:41,796 --> 00:31:45,758
I would like to ask
about your cat, Mr. Hyuga.

491
00:31:45,842 --> 00:31:47,468
-Nice to meet you.
-Likewise.

492
00:31:47,552 --> 00:31:50,013
-Please have a seat.
-Okay.

493
00:31:51,597 --> 00:31:56,019
-Well then, let's get started.
-Yes, please.

494
00:32:02,150 --> 00:32:04,610
You're Sho Shimoyama, right?

495
00:32:06,112 --> 00:32:09,282
I'm Aso, the lawyer
representing Mr. Shibata.

496
00:32:09,365 --> 00:32:11,159
Do you have some time?

497
00:32:15,496 --> 00:32:19,167
Mr. Shibata never told anyone
that you smoked.

498
00:32:20,543 --> 00:32:25,339
I think he believed you weren't a student
who would do something like that.

499
00:32:28,092 --> 00:32:32,138
Did someone force you to smoke?

500
00:32:34,515 --> 00:32:39,729
-Can we finish this by tomorrow?
-Do we get late-night overtime pay?

501
00:32:41,147 --> 00:32:42,648
No, but Mr. Kureta got us this.

502
00:32:43,232 --> 00:32:45,651
Hold on, sweets?

503
00:32:45,735 --> 00:32:47,862
Pretty sweet deal, right?

504
00:32:49,363 --> 00:32:52,325
Come on, don't say
bad puns with a straight face.

505
00:32:52,408 --> 00:32:57,455
Quit your late-night fooling around.
Get to work!

506
00:32:57,538 --> 00:33:01,250
Come on, do a Monaki dance for us!

507
00:33:01,334 --> 00:33:02,418
Guess I must.

508
00:33:05,213 --> 00:33:06,422
-Anyway, Nakazaki.
-Yeah?

509
00:33:06,506 --> 00:33:10,218
-You got the data from Hyuga's computer?
-I gave it to Mr. Uramawashi.

510
00:33:10,301 --> 00:33:11,844
-Really?
-Hey, look at my dance!

511
00:33:11,928 --> 00:33:15,640
-Show me later. I want to see it.
-Okay.

512
00:33:15,723 --> 00:33:17,517
-Forward it to me.
-Okay.

513
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:21,270
-Hey, dance, I want to see!
-Do you really?

514
00:33:21,354 --> 00:33:22,730
<i>I want to see!</i>

515
00:33:22,814 --> 00:33:25,191
<i>Then watch this time!</i>

516
00:33:27,026 --> 00:33:28,444
<i>Watch me!</i>

517
00:33:32,073 --> 00:33:36,285
SHIMOYAMA

518
00:33:39,288 --> 00:33:43,626
You again? No matter how many times
you come, nothing will change.

519
00:33:46,003 --> 00:33:47,588
I found this.

520
00:33:51,134 --> 00:33:52,718
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

521
00:33:55,513 --> 00:33:56,347
YUKIE SHIMOYAMA

522
00:33:56,430 --> 00:33:58,015
Mrs. Shimoyama,

523
00:33:58,099 --> 00:34:00,935
you were against the school merger
the whole time, weren't you?

524
00:34:04,313 --> 00:34:06,399
What really happened?

525
00:34:08,234 --> 00:34:12,321
I will definitely help you.
Please talk to me.

526
00:34:19,787 --> 00:34:22,957
-We've been expecting you. This way.
-Thank you.

527
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:26,919
-Thank you for coming.
-Quite a crowd.

528
00:34:27,003 --> 00:34:29,255
-Hello.
-This way.

529
00:34:29,338 --> 00:34:31,924
-Good morning.
-Morning.

530
00:34:34,760 --> 00:34:36,387
Today's materials.

531
00:34:36,470 --> 00:34:38,931
I'll hand them to the person in charge.

532
00:34:40,308 --> 00:34:41,517
Come in.

533
00:34:42,310 --> 00:34:45,146
-Pleasure working with you today.
-Likewise.

534
00:34:45,229 --> 00:34:48,816
I've prepared the script
and video materials right here.

535
00:34:49,650 --> 00:34:52,570
You're a great help.
Preparing materials is a pain.

536
00:34:52,653 --> 00:34:55,239
All that hard work pays off today.

537
00:34:56,240 --> 00:34:58,826
It's all going according
to Mr. Hyuga's plan.

538
00:34:59,660 --> 00:35:01,704
Trusting you was the right choice.

539
00:35:20,973 --> 00:35:22,433
Come in.

540
00:35:22,516 --> 00:35:23,726
Excuse me.

541
00:35:23,809 --> 00:35:27,563
The data you gave me earlier is playing
on the monitor now. Please check.

542
00:35:27,647 --> 00:35:29,273
-Okay.
-Okay.

543
00:35:29,357 --> 00:35:32,401
You keep checking.
I'm going to the restroom.

544
00:35:32,485 --> 00:35:33,736
Okay.

545
00:35:35,404 --> 00:35:38,032
Wait, it won't open!

546
00:35:38,115 --> 00:35:39,533
Let me look at it.

547
00:35:40,534 --> 00:35:41,786
<i>I heard back in your idol days,</i>

548
00:35:41,869 --> 00:35:44,330
<i>you had to sacrifice sleep,</i>
<i>and it was tough.</i>

549
00:35:44,413 --> 00:35:47,792
<i>Yeah. Everyone goes through that, right?</i>

550
00:35:47,875 --> 00:35:52,338
<i>You have a great track record as a leader,</i>
<i>Ms. Nijima.</i>

551
00:35:52,838 --> 00:35:56,759
<i>Of course. If I hadn't taken the lead</i>
<i>and pulled them along,</i>

552
00:35:56,842 --> 00:35:58,803
<i>nothing would have changed.</i>

553
00:35:58,886 --> 00:36:00,304
What is this?

554
00:36:00,388 --> 00:36:04,600
That's some great editing! You did great.

555
00:36:04,684 --> 00:36:06,602
I didn't do anything.

556
00:36:07,812 --> 00:36:11,315
<i>Do you think Takanashi Construction</i>
<i>can survive moving forward?</i>

557
00:36:11,399 --> 00:36:14,902
<i>If they don't adapt with the times,</i>
<i>they're just going to vanish.</i>

558
00:36:15,945 --> 00:36:18,030
This isn't what I was asked!

559
00:36:18,698 --> 00:36:23,119
<i>It's kind of embarrassing</i>
<i>to see them cling to outdated ways.</i>

560
00:36:23,202 --> 00:36:24,829
What is the meaning of this?

561
00:36:25,621 --> 00:36:27,581
It was just a magazine interview, I was…

562
00:36:27,665 --> 00:36:29,375
Don't play dumb!

563
00:36:29,458 --> 00:36:31,752
The question is about
Takanashi Construction!

564
00:36:31,836 --> 00:36:33,254
And you said you hate them!

565
00:36:33,337 --> 00:36:34,588
-Is that so?
-I didn't!

566
00:36:34,672 --> 00:36:35,798
Huh, that's me?

567
00:36:35,881 --> 00:36:39,176
<i>What's your take on the allegations</i>
<i>that Nijima is having affairs?</i>

568
00:36:39,260 --> 00:36:40,845
<i>She's for sure doing it.</i>

569
00:36:40,928 --> 00:36:43,848
<i>I can tell who has</i>
<i>by looking in their eyes.</i>

570
00:36:43,931 --> 00:36:46,892
-Wait, what is this?
<i>-So she won despite cheating?</i>

571
00:36:48,728 --> 00:36:51,147
<i>Well, you know, pillow talk is important.</i>

572
00:36:51,230 --> 00:36:53,649
<i>You mean Ms. Nijima slept around</i>
<i>to get promotions?</i>

573
00:36:53,733 --> 00:36:54,525
<i>That's right.</i>

574
00:36:55,109 --> 00:36:57,611
<i>The one who sleeps well wins.</i>

575
00:36:57,695 --> 00:36:59,405
No, come on…

576
00:36:59,488 --> 00:37:02,450
Is that what you think of me?

577
00:37:02,533 --> 00:37:05,745
<i>-I don't like that stuff.</i>
-Don't mess with me!

578
00:37:05,828 --> 00:37:10,333
<i>Well, I wouldn't mind trying, though.</i>
<i>I could get hooked.</i>

579
00:37:10,833 --> 00:37:14,128
I got it! I was talking
about secrets to good health!

580
00:37:14,211 --> 00:37:15,046
That hurts!

581
00:37:15,129 --> 00:37:18,674
You. What's the deal with this video?
Did you betray me?

582
00:37:18,758 --> 00:37:22,678
I don't know! I only handed
the materials for the meeting!

583
00:37:22,762 --> 00:37:25,014
I just plugged in the USB drive
I was given!

584
00:37:25,097 --> 00:37:27,892
-Then what about this…
-Just delete it!

585
00:37:27,975 --> 00:37:29,602
Delete it right now!

586
00:37:30,227 --> 00:37:33,981
<i>Were Ms. Nijima and President Takanashi</i>
<i>easy to handle?</i>

587
00:37:34,065 --> 00:37:39,070
<i>Yes. Dangle some bait in front of them,</i>
<i>and they'll do as you say.</i>

588
00:37:39,153 --> 00:37:42,198
<i>If so, does it mean they're not smart?</i>

589
00:37:42,281 --> 00:37:46,452
<i>Basically, they're incapable of</i>
<i>understanding anything complicated.</i>

590
00:37:49,413 --> 00:37:51,540
<i>They're good kids and really cute</i>

591
00:37:51,624 --> 00:37:54,377
<i>when they're eating</i>
<i>out of the palm of my hand.</i>

592
00:37:54,460 --> 00:37:55,795
Don't get violent.

593
00:37:55,878 --> 00:37:59,673
-I was talking about my cat.
-You were looking down on me, bastard!

594
00:37:59,757 --> 00:38:01,425
How dare you make a fool out of me?

595
00:38:01,509 --> 00:38:05,930
Hey, if I weren't here,
you guys wouldn't be able to do anything!

596
00:38:06,013 --> 00:38:07,014
You mock me!

597
00:38:07,098 --> 00:38:09,934
<i>She is so simple-minded,</i>
<i>it's kind of cute!</i>

598
00:38:10,017 --> 00:38:13,729
You airheaded idol-turned-politician!
Don't get cocky!

599
00:38:13,813 --> 00:38:16,232
And you exploit your employees
to line your own pockets!

600
00:38:16,816 --> 00:38:21,278
I'm fed up with how stupid you two are!

601
00:38:21,362 --> 00:38:24,115
Assembly Members
shouldn't be on reality shows!

602
00:38:24,198 --> 00:38:27,410
Assembly Members have freedom too!

603
00:38:39,338 --> 00:38:42,216
Dad! What are you doing?

604
00:38:46,387 --> 00:38:49,557
Everyone, this video is a fake!

605
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:51,684
It's all fabricated!

606
00:38:51,767 --> 00:38:55,312
Yes. Fake videos like these
are so easy to make!

607
00:38:56,313 --> 00:39:02,611
That abusive teacher, Shibata,
pulled strings to frame us!

608
00:39:02,695 --> 00:39:04,405
That's not true!

609
00:39:04,488 --> 00:39:07,116
My dad would never do
anything so cowardly!

610
00:39:07,783 --> 00:39:10,411
Even if he got violent,
there had to be a reason for it!

611
00:39:10,995 --> 00:39:14,748
You're his daughter.
Whatever you say is useless.

612
00:39:14,832 --> 00:39:19,753
The evidence of his violence
still remains in the video!

613
00:39:19,837 --> 00:39:24,008
-Well, there are videos of you guys too!
-Yeah!

614
00:39:24,091 --> 00:39:27,928
I told you, this is all fake!

615
00:39:28,596 --> 00:39:30,306
We can say that too!

616
00:39:34,977 --> 00:39:37,146
Mr. Shibata is the victim here!

617
00:39:37,229 --> 00:39:41,525
That video
was intentionally filmed to frame him!

618
00:39:42,318 --> 00:39:43,611
Mom…

619
00:39:43,694 --> 00:39:46,489
It's true, right?

620
00:39:49,408 --> 00:39:50,868
My son…

621
00:39:51,785 --> 00:39:55,122
Because I'm frail and can't work,

622
00:39:55,873 --> 00:40:01,504
he accepted money to pretend to smoke
in front of Mr. Shibata.

623
00:40:03,506 --> 00:40:06,091
But the fact remains
that he hit him, right?

624
00:40:06,759 --> 00:40:07,801
Right?

625
00:40:17,770 --> 00:40:18,979
Sho…

626
00:40:21,106 --> 00:40:24,944
It's meaningless
to obtain things through lies.

627
00:40:32,326 --> 00:40:34,245
-He didn't hit me.
-Sho!

628
00:40:34,328 --> 00:40:36,038
I don't want to lie anymore!

629
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:46,382
Mr. Shibata just took away the cigarette,
and I pretended to be hit and fell over.

630
00:40:47,216 --> 00:40:49,093
The bruise I had back then

631
00:40:50,052 --> 00:40:52,638
was because Taiga hit me.

632
00:40:59,228 --> 00:41:02,481
I am truly, deeply sorry.

633
00:41:03,941 --> 00:41:07,403
I will apologize to Mr. Shibata too.

634
00:41:08,445 --> 00:41:12,449
I am so sorry.

635
00:41:36,140 --> 00:41:37,349
You…

636
00:41:37,433 --> 00:41:38,517
You were the one

637
00:41:38,601 --> 00:41:42,855
who advised President Takanashi
and Ms. Nijima on this plan.

638
00:41:47,067 --> 00:41:49,320
What?

639
00:41:50,362 --> 00:41:53,574
Where is your proof?

640
00:41:57,911 --> 00:41:58,746
What?

641
00:42:00,956 --> 00:42:03,292
What a pain in the ass.

642
00:42:03,375 --> 00:42:04,793
ITABASHI WARD REDEVELOPMENT BID

643
00:42:04,877 --> 00:42:10,007
I have records of you commissioning
the fake video and paying for it,

644
00:42:10,716 --> 00:42:12,468
along with other proof of your corruption.

645
00:42:13,761 --> 00:42:16,096
How did you get your hands on this?

646
00:42:18,557 --> 00:42:23,437
You probably used
illegal means again, didn't you?

647
00:42:24,480 --> 00:42:28,275
In the end, you're nothing
more than that murderer's--

648
00:42:32,071 --> 00:42:34,782
Careless words invite ruin.

649
00:42:37,326 --> 00:42:40,120
I'll make sure you never defend again.

650
00:42:45,918 --> 00:42:48,128
You'd better watch your mouth.

651
00:42:54,551 --> 00:42:56,970
Murderer?

652
00:43:02,685 --> 00:43:05,562
After the incident, Ms. Nijima resigned.

653
00:43:05,646 --> 00:43:08,816
Takanashi Construction is also pulling out
of the public works projects.

654
00:43:09,692 --> 00:43:11,110
Great job out there.

655
00:43:13,529 --> 00:43:19,243
By the way, just to confirm,
Mr. Uramawashi wasn't involved, right?

656
00:43:29,628 --> 00:43:31,714
I'm sorry. Please don't ask.

657
00:43:31,797 --> 00:43:34,091
That's pretty much an answer right there.

658
00:43:34,633 --> 00:43:37,678
SUPER VIRAL WATCH

659
00:43:37,761 --> 00:43:39,430
The likes keep going up!

660
00:43:39,513 --> 00:43:44,393
-True.
-Our late-night editing was worth it.

661
00:43:44,476 --> 00:43:48,480
-Let's make a video of you next.
-Stop it!

662
00:43:48,564 --> 00:43:51,066
-Don't do it.
-Boss.

663
00:43:51,150 --> 00:43:53,152
The receipts I promised you.

664
00:43:53,235 --> 00:43:55,988
Damn it, I thought I was going to win!

665
00:43:56,071 --> 00:43:57,531
What's this?

666
00:43:57,614 --> 00:44:00,075
We had a bet on whether
Ms. Aso would make it in time.

667
00:44:00,159 --> 00:44:01,577
Excuse me!

668
00:44:02,286 --> 00:44:05,122
Ms. Aso, good morning.

669
00:44:07,624 --> 00:44:13,422
I had a hunch you were scheming something.
Why didn't you tell me?

670
00:44:13,964 --> 00:44:18,886
You can't tell a lie.
You would have told them everything.

671
00:44:20,471 --> 00:44:25,017
But you said you stored
the lies away in the basement!

672
00:44:26,643 --> 00:44:29,563
My house is single-story.

673
00:44:29,646 --> 00:44:31,064
What?

674
00:44:32,024 --> 00:44:35,527
This is why I hate lies.

675
00:44:36,570 --> 00:44:38,530
I'm grateful to you, Aso.

676
00:44:38,614 --> 00:44:39,448
Huh?

677
00:44:40,157 --> 00:44:43,577
You brought Sho Shimoyama's
mother to the school.

678
00:44:45,996 --> 00:44:48,916
Keep doing your best without lying.

679
00:44:49,625 --> 00:44:52,419
No need to tell me.

680
00:44:52,503 --> 00:44:56,131
Also, it looks like the school merger
will be scrapped.

681
00:44:56,215 --> 00:44:59,635
-The violence charge will be dropped too.
-A moment, Mr. Uramawashi?

682
00:45:07,100 --> 00:45:09,269
Sorry!

683
00:45:12,481 --> 00:45:13,690
What?

684
00:45:19,571 --> 00:45:21,865
JUSTICE'S FORM

685
00:45:23,534 --> 00:45:24,576
LEARN THE LAW, BUT DOUBT IT

686
00:45:26,495 --> 00:45:30,582
THE LAW ISN'T ALWAYS RIGHT
FIND YOUR OWN JUSTICE

687
00:45:32,251 --> 00:45:34,920
MIYUKI SHIRAMOTO
BORN 1981, KANAGAWA

688
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:48,016
<i>Nice to meet you, woof!</i>

689
00:45:49,851 --> 00:45:51,645
You must remain silent.

690
00:45:52,312 --> 00:45:55,190
<i>They had Public Security plant evidence?</i>

691
00:45:56,316 --> 00:45:57,985
<i>We'll remake the lie.</i>

692
00:45:58,068 --> 00:46:01,738
-Hey!
<i>-Intruders detected.</i>

693
00:46:02,322 --> 00:46:07,202
Shall I show you
the moment your lies crumble?

694
00:46:07,286 --> 00:46:08,245
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

